    <h1>
      The <code style="font-size: .8em; background: none; border: 0; padding: 0">quorum</code> crate
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The decision core of the shrinking quorum. Each tick it decides what the system may deliver, given what three
      replicas returned. It also chooses one value from up to three sensor readings of the same quantity.
    </p>
    <div class="row" style="gap: 8px; margin: 8px 0 24px">
      <span class="pill">no_std</span>
      <span class="pill">no allocation</span>
      <span class="pill">no dependencies</span>
      <span class="pill sig">
        <span class="dot"></span>9 Kani proofs, 16 with the C interface
      </span>
      <span class="pill">v0.9.0</span>
    </div>

    <h2 id="install">Install</h2>
    <p>
      The crate is not on crates.io. Its manifest sets <code>publish = false</code>. Depend on the repository at a tag:
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0"><span class="c"># Cargo.toml</span>
[dependencies]
quorum = {'{'} git = <span class="s">"https://github.com/mruspace/flight"</span>, tag = <span class="s">"v0.9.0"</span> {'}'}</pre>

    <h2 id="example">Example</h2>
    <pre
      class="pre"
      tabindex="0"
    ><span class="k">use</span> quorum::{'{'}decide, Health, Outcome, Policy, Reply, REPLICAS{'}'};

<span class="c">// read_replicas, send and run_known_answer_test are your code.</span>
<span class="k">let mut</span> health = Health::new();
<span class="k">for</span> tick <span class="k">in</span> 0u64.. {'{'}
    <span class="k">let</span> replies: [Reply; REPLICAS] = read_replicas(tick);
    <span class="k">let</span> v = decide(Policy::Shrink, &amp;replies);

    <span class="k">if let</span> <span class="s">Outcome::Deliver</span>(x) = v.outcome {'{'} send(x); {'}'}
    <span class="k">for</span> (i, outvoted) <span class="k">in</span> v.dissent.iter().enumerate() {'{'}
        <span class="k">if</span> *outvoted &amp;&amp; health.strike(i, tick) {'{'} run_known_answer_test(i); {'}'}
    {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>

    <h2 id="gate">Gate commands on the mode</h2>
    <p>
      On one replica, self-check can deliver a few wrong results before the periodic known-answer test catches a stuck
      fault. Use that mode for data products, not spacecraft commands, unless the mission adds its own command safety
      layer. This example issues a command only when the mode is <code>Vote</code> or <code>Compare</code> and the
      outcome is <code>Deliver</code>. See <a href="/concepts/shrinking-quorum/#command-path">Command path</a>.
    </p>
    <pre
      class="pre"
      tabindex="0"
    ><span class="c">//! Gate commands on the mode. Only a result that two or more replicas agree</span>
<span class="c">//! on (vote or compare) may command the spacecraft. A result from the last</span>
<span class="c">//! replica&#39;s self-check goes out as a data product only.</span>
<span class="k">use</span> quorum::{'{'}decide, Mode, Outcome, Policy, Reply, REPLICAS{'}'};

<span class="c">/// What to do with one tick&#39;s result.</span>
<span class="k">enum</span> Action {'{'}
    <span class="c">/// Agreed by two or more replicas: may be used as a command.</span>
    Command(u64),
    <span class="c">/// Self-check on the last replica: data product only.</span>
    Data(u64),
    <span class="c">/// Nothing to send this tick.</span>
    Hold,
{'}'}

<span class="k">fn</span> gate(replies: &amp;[Reply; REPLICAS]) -&gt; Action {'{'}
    <span class="k">let</span> verdict = decide(Policy::Shrink, replies);
    <span class="k">match</span> (verdict.mode, verdict.outcome) {'{'}
        (Mode::Vote | Mode::Compare, Outcome::Deliver(x)) =&gt; Action::Command(x),
        (Mode::SelfCheck, Outcome::Deliver(x)) =&gt; Action::Data(x),
        _ =&gt; Action::Hold,
    {'}'}
{'}'}

<span class="k">fn</span> main() {'{'}
    <span class="k">use</span> Reply::{'{'}Absent, Pair, Single{'}'};
    <span class="k">let</span> ticks = [
        [Single(7), Single(7), Single(9)], <span class="c">// vote: two agree on 7</span>
        [Absent, Single(7), Single(7)],    <span class="c">// compare: both say 7</span>
        [Absent, Single(7), Single(9)],    <span class="c">// compare: mismatch</span>
        [Absent, Absent, Pair(7, 7)],      <span class="c">// self-check on the last replica</span>
        [Absent, Absent, Absent],          <span class="c">// nothing left</span>
    ];
    <span class="k">for</span> replies <span class="k">in</span> &amp;ticks {'{'}
        <span class="k">match</span> gate(replies) {'{'}
            Action::Command(x) =&gt; println!("{'{'}replies:?{'}'}: command {'{'}x{'}'}"),
            Action::Data(x) =&gt; println!("{'{'}replies:?{'}'}: data product {'{'}x{'}'}"),
            Action::Hold =&gt; println!("{'{'}replies:?{'}'}: hold"),
        {'}'}
    {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      Its output, from <code>cargo run</code> against v0.9.0:
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">[Single(7), Single(7), Single(9)]: command 7
[Absent, Single(7), Single(7)]: command 7
[Absent, Single(7), Single(9)]: hold
[Absent, Absent, Pair(7, 7)]: data product 7
[Absent, Absent, Absent]: hold</pre>

    <h2 id="api">API</h2>
    <h3>const REPLICAS: usize = 3</h3>
    <p>Number of replicas.</p>
    <h3>const STRIKES: usize = 3</h3>
    <p>
      Strikes within <code>STRIKE_WINDOW</code> ticks that trigger a diagnosis.
    </p>
    <h3>const STRIKE_WINDOW: u64 = 200</h3>
    <p>Length of the strike window, in ticks.</p>

    <h3>enum Policy</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Shrink</td>
            <td>Vote on three, compare on two, self-check on one.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Tmr</td>
            <td>Vote on three, compare on two, stop on one (classic fixed TMR).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>enum Mode</h3>
    <p>
      <code>Vote</code>, <code>Compare</code>, <code>SelfCheck</code> (one replica computes everything twice and
      compares with itself), <code>Halted</code>.
    </p>

    <h3>enum Reply</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Absent</td>
            <td>The replica is dead or did not answer.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Single(u64)</td>
            <td>One result.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Pair(u64, u64)</td>
            <td>Two results of the same computation (self-check).</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>enum Outcome</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr class="hl">
            <td class="m">Deliver(u64)</td>
            <td>Deliver this result.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Detected</td>
            <td>A disagreement was caught; deliver nothing this tick.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Halted</td>
            <td>The policy cannot continue with the replicas left.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>struct Verdict</h3>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">mode</td>
            <td class="m">Mode</td>
            <td>The mode used this tick.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">outcome</td>
            <td class="m">Outcome</td>
            <td>What to do with this tick.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">dissent</td>
            <td class="m">[bool; 3]</td>
            <td>Replicas that were outvoted (vote mode only).</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">diagnose</td>
            <td class="m">bool</td>
            <td>
              Two replicas disagree and nothing tells which is wrong: run a known-answer test on both (shrinking quorum
              only).
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>fn mode(policy, alive) -&gt; Mode</h3>
    <p>
      The mode a policy runs in with <code>alive</code> live replicas.
    </p>
    <h3>fn decide(policy, &amp;[Reply; 3]) -&gt; Verdict</h3>
    <p>Decide what to deliver from the replicas&#39; replies.</p>
    <h3>struct Health</h3>
    <p>
      Strike record per replica. <code>Health::new()</code> is <code>const</code>. <code>strike(i, tick)</code> returns{' '}
      <code>true</code> when replica <code>i</code> has three strikes inside the window and must be diagnosed.{' '}
      <code>clear(i)</code> forgets its strikes after it passes. <code>to_raw()</code> and{' '}
      <code>Health::from_raw(strikes, count)</code> turn the record into plain arrays and back, to save it across a
      reset or hand it to C.
    </p>
    <p>
      From C or C++, use the <a href="/core/fprime/#c">C interface</a>, <code>quorum.h</code>. Kani proves that{' '}
      <code>quorum_mode</code>, <code>quorum_decide</code>, <code>quorum_health_strike</code>,{' '}
      <code>quorum_health_clear</code>, <code>quorum_sensor_select</code> and <code>quorum_sensor_observe</code> give
      this crate&#39;s answer. The last two are the C side of <a href="#sensor">sensor selection</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sensor">Sensor selection</h2>
    <p>
      <code>decide()</code> needs results that match exactly. Readings of one quantity by three sensors never do: noise,
      calibration and timing make them differ a little. The module <code>quorum::sensor</code> compares readings within
      a tolerance, <code>tol</code>, in the same units as the readings.
    </p>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Readings in</th>
            <th>Value chosen</th>
            <th>Otherwise</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Three</td>
            <td>
              The median, if at least one other reading is within <code>tol</code> of it.
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>Disagree</code>: nothing delivered.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Two</td>
            <td>
              Their midpoint, rounded down, if they are within <code>tol</code> of each other.
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>Disagree</code>: nothing says which is right, so nothing is delivered.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>One</td>
            <td>
              The reading, as <code>Unchecked</code>, since nothing checks it.
            </td>
            <td>Not applicable.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>None</td>
            <td>
              <code>Nothing</code>.
            </td>
            <td>Not applicable.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="tiny">From the module comment and select() in quorum/src/sensor.rs at v0.9.0.</p>
    <p>
      With three readings and an agreed value, a reading more than <code>tol</code> from that value is an outlier.{' '}
      <code>observe()</code> separates a short spike from a sensor that has failed: it excludes a sensor only after{' '}
      <code>limit</code> outlier cycles in a row. Pass <code>None</code> for an excluded sensor.
    </p>
    <p>
      The F&#180; component <code>SensorVoter</code> calls this module through <code>quorum_sensor_select</code>. It has
      run in the OPS-SAT run 4 package on the ground, not in orbit. The module does not make every replica&#39;s input
      equal before the replicas compute. That step is not built.
    </p>

    <h3>const SENSORS: usize = 3</h3>
    <p>Number of sensors of one quantity.</p>

    <h3>enum Selected</h3>
    <p>
      What <code>select</code> chose.
    </p>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <tbody>
          <tr class="hl">
            <td class="m">Agreed(i32)</td>
            <td>A value two or more readings agree on, within the tolerance.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Unchecked(i32)</td>
            <td>The only reading: not cross-checked.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Disagree</td>
            <td>
              The readings differ by more than the tolerance and nothing says which one is right. Nothing is delivered.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">Nothing</td>
            <td>No reading.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>struct Selection</h3>
    <p>The choice for one cycle.</p>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Field</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Meaning</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">selected</td>
            <td class="m">Selected</td>
            <td>The value chosen, or why there is none.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">outlier</td>
            <td class="m">[bool; 3]</td>
            <td>
              Readings more than the tolerance away from the agreed value. Set only when three readings give{' '}
              <code>Selected::Agreed</code>.
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h3>fn close(a: i32, b: i32, tol: u32) -&gt; bool</h3>
    <p>
      Whether two readings are within <code>tol</code> of each other, with no overflow.
    </p>
    <h3>fn select(readings: &amp;[Option&lt;i32&gt;; SENSORS], tol: u32) -&gt; Selection</h3>
    <p>
      Choose one value from the readings of the sensors in use (<code>None</code>: no reading, or a sensor excluded),
      with tolerance <code>tol</code>.
    </p>
    <h3>fn observe(run: u8, outlier: bool, limit: u8) -&gt; (u8, bool)</h3>
    <p>
      One cycle of a sensor&#39;s outlier count: <code>run</code> is its outlier cycles in a row so far. Returns the new
      count, and whether the sensor must now be excluded: after <code>limit</code> outlier cycles in a row (never when{' '}
      <code>limit</code> is 0). Call it only in cycles with an agreed value; in others, keep the count.
    </p>

    <h3 id="sensor-example">Example</h3>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0"><span class="k">use</span> quorum::sensor::{'{'}observe, select{'}'};

<span class="k">fn</span> main() {'{'}
    <span class="k">let</span> tol = 10;
    <span class="k">let</span> cycles = [
        [Some(100), Some(104), Some(98)],  <span class="c">// three agree: the median</span>
        [Some(100), Some(5000), Some(98)], <span class="c">// a spike on sensor 1</span>
        [Some(100), None, Some(105)],      <span class="c">// two agree: the midpoint</span>
        [Some(100), None, Some(200)],      <span class="c">// two disagree</span>
        [None, Some(7), None],             <span class="c">// one reading</span>
    ];
    <span class="k">for</span> r <span class="k">in</span> &amp;cycles {'{'}
        <span class="k">let</span> s = select(r, tol);
        println!("{'{'}r:?{'}'}: {'{'}:?{'}'} {'{'}:?{'}'}", s.selected, s.outlier);
    {'}'}

    <span class="c">// Exclude a sensor after 3 outlier cycles in a row.</span>
    <span class="k">let mut</span> run = 0;
    <span class="k">for</span> outlier <span class="k">in</span> [true, true, false, true, true, true] {'{'}
        <span class="k">let</span> (r, exclude) = observe(run, outlier, 3);
        run = r;
        println!("outlier {'{'}outlier{'}'}: run {'{'}run{'}'}, exclude {'{'}exclude{'}'}");
    {'}'}
{'}'}</pre>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      Its output, from <code>cargo run</code> against v0.9.0:
    </p>
    <pre class="pre" tabindex="0">[Some(100), Some(104), Some(98)]: Agreed(100) [false, false, false]
[Some(100), Some(5000), Some(98)]: Agreed(100) [false, true, false]
[Some(100), None, Some(105)]: Agreed(102) [false, false, false]
[Some(100), None, Some(200)]: Disagree [false, false, false]
[None, Some(7), None]: Unchecked(7) [false, false, false]
outlier true: run 1, exclude false
outlier true: run 2, exclude false
outlier false: run 0, exclude false
outlier true: run 1, exclude false
outlier true: run 2, exclude false
outlier true: run 3, exclude true</pre>

    <h2 id="proofs">Kani proofs</h2>
    <p>
      16 proofs in the workspace. Nine are on the crate: four on <code>decide()</code> and five on sensor selection in
      <code>quorum::sensor</code>. Seven are on the C interface in <code>quorum-ffi</code>. CI runs
      <code>cargo kani -p quorum -p quorum-ffi</code> on every change. On the v0.9.0 commit it verified all 16, with 0
      failures. In the <code>decide()</code> proofs, each reply is any of <code>Absent</code>, <code>Single</code> or
      <code>Pair</code>, with any <code>u64</code> values.
    </p>
    <div class="tbl-box" tabindex="0">
      <table class="tbl">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Proof</th>
            <th>Property</th>
            <th>Scope</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/lib.rs#L334">
                identical_while_tmr_can_run
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>With two or more replies present, both policies give the same outcome.</td>
            <td>
              Every set of three replies with two or more present. Outcome only, not mode or <code>diagnose</code>.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/lib.rs#L346">tmr_stops_below_two</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              With fewer than two replies present, fixed TMR&#39;s outcome is <code>Halted</code>.
            </td>
            <td>Every set of three replies with fewer than two present.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/lib.rs#L355">
                shrink_halts_only_with_nothing_left
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              The shrinking quorum&#39;s outcome is <code>Halted</code> if and only if no reply is present.
            </td>
            <td>Every set of three replies.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/lib.rs#L365">
                delivers_only_agreed_values
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              A delivered value has two agreeing replies, or exactly one replica alive that returned{' '}
              <code>Pair(v, v)</code>.
            </td>
            <td>Every set of three replies, under both policies.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/sensor.rs#L230">
                agreed_values_are_agreed_and_in_range
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              An agreed value has at least two readings within the tolerance of it, and lies between the smallest and
              the largest reading.
            </td>
            <td>
              Every set of three readings, each absent or any <code>i32</code>, and every tolerance.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/sensor.rs#L254">
                outliers_are_never_chosen
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              An outlier is a reading of an agreed cycle more than the tolerance away from the value chosen, so it is
              never the value delivered. With three readings in, every other reading is within the tolerance.
            </td>
            <td>
              Every set of three readings, each absent or any <code>i32</code>, and every tolerance.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/sensor.rs#L279">
                median_is_the_median
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              The median of three is one of the three values, with at least two of them on each side of it (itself
              counted).
            </td>
            <td>
              Every three <code>i32</code> values, ties included.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/sensor.rs#L291">
                unchecked_only_with_one_reading
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>Unchecked</code> comes only from exactly one reading, and <code>Nothing</code> only from none. Every
              other result has two or more readings in.
            </td>
            <td>
              Every set of three readings, each absent or any <code>i32</code>, and every tolerance.
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum/src/sensor.rs#L306">
                excluded_only_after_limit_outliers_in_a_row
              </a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>observe</code> excludes a sensor exactly when its last <code>limit</code> cycles were all outliers.
              A spike shorter than the limit never excludes it.
            </td>
            <td>Every limit from 1 to 6, every sequence of six cycles.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
              <a href="https://github.com/mruspace/flight/blob/v0.9.0/quorum-ffi/src/lib.rs#L441">decide_is_the_core</a>
            </td>
            <td>
              <code>quorum_decide</code> gives the core&#39;s verdict. An unknown reply kind counts as absent.
            </td>
            <td>C interface: policy 0 or 1, any reply kind and values.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="m">
