    <p class="tiny">Each proof name links to its source at v0.9.0.</p>
    <h3 id="not-covered">Not covered</h3>
    <ul class="sig-list">
      <li>
        <strong>
          <code>Health</code> in the core.
        </strong>{' '}
        Unit tests only.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Diagnosis and the known-answer test.</strong> They run in the demo and in F&#180;, not in the core.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Timing.</strong> The proofs say what <code>decide()</code> returns, not how long it takes. The
        <a href="/core/bench/#core">bench</a> measures that.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The system over a run.</strong> Never less than fixed TMR over a whole run is tested, not proved. See
        <a href="/concepts/shrinking-quorum/#tested">Tested (per run)</a>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Sensor values against the truth.</strong> The proofs say which reading <code>select()</code> chooses,
        not how close it is to the true value. The F&#180; test component <code>SensorSim</code> scores that.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="targets">Targets and builds</h2>
    <p>CI builds and tests on every change:</p>
    <ul class="sig-list">
      <li>Linux ARM64, Linux x86_64 and macOS (Apple silicon)</li>
      <li>
        Bare-metal ARM Cortex-M, <code>thumbv7em-none-eabihf</code>, as <code>no_std</code> (build only)
      </li>
      <li>
        Static Linux binaries of the demo and the bench: 64-bit ARM, 32-bit ARM (hard and soft float) and x86_64. CI
        runs the scenario tests on each in a container, the ARM ones under emulation.
      </li>
      <li>
        The F&#180; components and deployments, which call the crate through <code>quorum.h</code>: build, unit tests
        and end-to-end runs
      </li>
      <li>
        The native cFS mission (cFE, OSAL and PSP of cFS v7.0.1, and the Mru app), which also calls the crate through{' '}
        <code>quorum.h</code>. CI builds it and runs it in the run 4 package.
      </li>
    </ul>
